{
  "abstract": "A Lean 4 / Mathlib proof of the main results of Yang, Yau and Yin, \"Delocalization and quantum diffusion of random band matrices in high dimensions I: Self-energy renormalization\" (arXiv:2104.12048), proved together with part \"II: T-expansion\" (arXiv:2107.05795). The model is the Gaussian random band matrix on the torus Z_L^d with band width W and a variance profile given by a symmetric Schwartz function, for L^{c_1} <= W <= L^{1-c_0}. For every dimension d >= 8: Theorem 1.3 of part I (weak delocalization of the bulk eigenvectors, (1.12) and (1.13)), Theorem 1.4 (the local law (1.19), down to eta = W^2 / L^{2-eps}), and Theorem 1.5 with Corollaries 1.6 and 1.7 (quantum diffusion: the expansion of E T_{xy} and E|G_{xy}|^2 with the renormalized diffusive matrix, the bounds on the self-energies, and the diffusion approximation in Fourier space). No result of another work is assumed; every result that the papers use is proved in the library from Mathlib.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Jun Yin"
    }
  ],
